  79: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
  80:     """
  81:     Draw same-colored rectangular connector bands through background channels between four matching marker blocks.
  82: 
  83:     Input structure
  84:     - A background lattice of separated framed tiles; the frame color is the unique most frequent non-background color.
  85:     - Each tile region contains one solid non-frame interior block.
  86:     - The unique most common interior color is the default; every other interior color marks four rectangle corners.
  87: 
  88:     Rule
  89:     - For each marker color, find its two row bands and two column bands.
  90:     - Paint that color through background cells along the two horizontal and two vertical sides of the implied rectangle.
  91:     - Preserve all original frame, default interior, marker, and off-path background pixels.
  92: 
  93:     Key insight
  94:     - The repeated tile frames define which cells are obstacles and which cells are background channels; matching interior colors supply rectangle corners independent of tile and marker size.
  95:     """
